        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "***Goal***\r",
          "\r",
          "This notebook introduces important graph algorithms available in Oracle AI Database 26ai.\r",
          "\r",
          "**You will learn how to:**\r",
          "\r",
          "- Use SQL graph analytics and PGX algorithms, including PageRank and weakly connected components (WCC).\r",
          "- Use the PGX Python API for DeepWalk, betweenness centrality, and closeness centrality.\r",
          "- Identify potential fraud patterns, bridge accounts, and major account clusters.\r",
          "\r",
          "**Some Questions explored in this notebook:**\r",
          "\r",
          "- How many weakly connected components are in `BANK_GRAPH`?\r",
          "- Which accounts receive the most transfers?\r",
          "- Which accounts are most influential in the payment network?\r",
          "- How are accounts 934, 387, and 135 connected through transfers?\r",
          "- Which accounts have transfer patterns similar to accounts 934 and 387?\r",
          "- Which accounts act as bridges between major clusters?\r",
          "- Which accounts have the most circular payment chains?\r",
          "- More..."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
